  chef: {fileID: 11400000, guid: d4ca161307a19ab499b5d49387c6380d, type: 2}
  letterBody: 'Hey again!


    Dan here. My waitress, Darlene, read about your place
    and asked me to send you her grandma''s recipe. Darlene has worked at my diner
    for twenty-two years, so when she asks, I listen.


    Peach cobbler isn''t
    fancy. Ripe peaches, a buttery batter poured over the top, baked until the edges
    go golden and the fruit bubbles through.


    Serve it warm. Ice cream if you''ve
    got it.


    The best recipes in my diner came from the people who work there.
    Remember to ask yours.'
